## 2. Terra claim 7 ("red reproduction — FALSE") — CORRECTED. The reds are HONEST.

Terra checked out the pre-fix parent f8b4b76 WHOLESALE. That deletes the
test blocks this opus added (lifecycle.test.ts blocks 42/43/44,
rules.test.ts blocks 16-19), so each recorded command ran a file with no
W-039 assertions in it and trivially exited 0. The result measures the
method, not the evidence.

Correct method (W-034 round 1 precedent): parent SOURCE + branch TEST files.

    git worktree add --detach .worktrees/censor-W-039-red f8b4b76
    git checkout 3be0a0b -- packages/cli/src/lifecycle.test.ts packages/cli/src/rules.test.ts
    grep -c namedSella packages/commands/src/lifecycle.ts   -> 0   (source is pre-fix)
    grep -c red_sella  packages/cli/src/rules/evidence.ts   -> 0
    grep -c red_sella  packages/cli/src/rules/ids.ts        -> 0

Result — every one of the seven recorded reds reproduces, exit 1, and the
body is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the recorded log after stripping the 7-line
header:

    red 01  BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR=42 node --import tsx packages/cli/src/lifecycle.test.ts .   exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 02  BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR=43 node --import tsx packages/cli/src/lifecycle.test.ts .   exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 03  BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR=44 node --import tsx packages/cli/src/lifecycle.test.ts .   exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 04  node --import tsx packages/cli/src/rules.test.ts . 16                                exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 05  node --import tsx packages/cli/src/rules.test.ts . 17                                exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 06  node --import tsx packages/cli/src/rules.test.ts . 18                                exit 1  IDENTICAL
    red 07  node --import tsx packages/cli/src/rules.test.ts . 19                                exit 1  IDENTICAL

The recorded `# command:` for 01-03 carries no selector, so it was also run
literally (whole file, no BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR): exit 1 with exactly 14
FAIL lines, all of them W-039's, and no other block failing.

These logs could not have been written by post-fix code. 01 records the
pre-fix fallback (`red-sella b1: no --sella, no env -> exits 2   0` — it
returned 0, and the preseeded directory was overwritten); 03 records the
pre-fix `"" ?? env` hole (`header names builder-b   # sella: ` — empty).
Both are behaviours the fixed source cannot produce.

