## 6. Advisory notes (none blocking, none requiring a fix round)

  N1. Reds 01-03 record `# command: node --import tsx packages/cli/src/lifecycle.test.ts .`
      with no behaviour selector, because lifecycle.test.ts selects blocks
      through the BISELLIUM_ONLY_BEHAVIOUR environment variable, not argv,
      and `red` records only the command after `--`. Class: 3 instances
      (studio/ci/reds/W-039/01.log, 02.log, 03.log line 2); rules.test.ts's
      reds 04-07 carry their selector correctly because that harness reads
      argv. The brief's "name that number in the # command:" was therefore
      not satisfiable as written for this file. Harmless here — the literal
      command reproduces the red, and opus.red_content compares bodies, which
      differ — but it is exactly the `# command:` provenance class the brief
      already routes to W-048.

  N2. `namedSella` (packages/commands/src/lifecycle.ts:53) selects on the
      trimmed value but returns the RAW one, so `--sella "  builder-a  "`
      records a padded header. Out of the matrix, untested, and consistent
      with `resolveSella`, which does not trim either; `opus.red_sella` trims
      before comparing, so a padded real sella does not trip the advisory.
      Single instance. Not worth a round.

  N3. RED_USAGE (packages/commands/src/lifecycle.ts:438) and the top-level
      usage banner still print `[--sella <id>]`. Still literally true — the
      env var satisfies the requirement — and the refusal message names the
      fix, so a user recovers in one step. Single instance. Note only.

## 7. Spec conformance

  Piece 1 — namedSella is a sibling of resolveSella, unexported, reads
  process.env once, empty/whitespace unset in both places, last-wins
  inherited from parseFlags. The refusal sits after safeRedsDir and before
  the tree hash / runCapture / mkdirSync; behaviours 1-2 prove byte for byte
  that a refused call leaves a preseeded 01.log and sibling 02.log untouched
  and writes no marker. All nine matrix rows are covered: rows 1-4 and the
  two whitespace rows by behaviours 1-2, rows 5-8 by behaviour 3, row 9 by
  behaviour 1's second half.

  Piece 2 — opus.red_sella is folded into checkRedEvidence, reads the
  existing logTexts map and parseLogHeader, adds no directory read and no
  parser, fires once per opus with the exact `where: ci/reds/<id>/` and
  message shape, names basenames in ascending order (logTexts is filled
  1..n, so insertion order is sorted), and is level "advise". Reach is the
  ACTIVE set only (evidence.ts:165), as the brief ruled. Off-contract files
  are excluded structurally rather than by a filter, because logTexts only
  ever holds 1..n.

  Registry — "opus.red_sella" is in RULE_IDS sorted between
  "opus.red_evidence" and "opus.sella", in the same commit as the rule
  (b6774bf); 126 -> 127.

  Acceptance — all four clauses met; clause 4 was declared void by the brief.

